  "last_executor_claim": "Report written to `/app/report.md`. Summary of what's in it:\n\n**Key findings from the corpus:**\n- **Adoption is broad but shallow** — 88% of orgs use AI somewhere, but only ~⅓ have scaled it and just 39% see EBIT impact (McKinsey, D0074). The pilot-to-scale gap is the biggest risk to a 68% revenue CAGR.\n- **Capital is flowing** — AI-agent startups raised billions last year (VoiceRun's $5.5M seed; OpenAI/Torch acquisition; MergeLabs' $250M seed at $850M valuation in healthcare AI).\n- **Infrastructure boom** — Stargate ($100B→$500B), Microsoft's ~$80B data-center plan; AI capex is visibly propping up US GDP.\n- **Bubble risk is mainstream** — AI investment reportedly ~17x pre-dotcom levels; worth preparing a defense slide.\n- **Regulatory flags** — EU AI Act transparency obligations for high-risk systems; fragmented global approaches (EU broad, US sectoral, Brazil/Singapore principles-based); UNCTAD16 digital-economy ministerial and Trump-era tech interventions (TikTok EO, Stargate backing).\n\n**On your projections:** directionally consistent with a scaling market, but I flagged lean R&D salary lines against the ongoing talent war, flat 74% margin without compute-cost validation, and zero taxes at $7.1M net income.\n\n**Main limitation:** your `tex.pdf` is a template with placeholder TAM/CAGR, and the corpus has no single \"global AI market size\" figure — you'll need to source that number separately or build it bottom-up from the segment-level GVR data I cited.",
